R <- c("# Results", "",
sprintf("The analysis included %s singleton live births and %s preterm births (%s%%) in the 26 urban concentrations (%d municipalities) over %s days (Table 1). Dispersion ranged from %s to %s across concentrations, and the estimated coefficient of the delivery-risk weight ranged from %s to %s (reported as a diagnostic only).", n_(n_nv), n_(n_ptb), f1(100 * n_ptb / n_nv), nrow(mun), n_(n_dias), f2(min(phi)), f2(max(phi)), f2(min(gama)), f2(max(gama))), "",
sprintf("The pooled cumulative exposure–response curve was close to flat (Figure 1). The pooled MRT was %s °C (%sth percentile of the pooled axis; 95%% CI, %s–%s °C, which spanned the entire search range). Compared with the MRT, the RR was %s at the 99th percentile (%s °C) and %s at the 1st percentile (%s °C) (Table 2). Secondary contrasts at the 95th, 90th, 10th, and 5th percentiles ranged from %s to %s, and none of the pooled relative risks excluded the null.",
        f1(tc$tmr), f1(100 * tc$percentil_tmr), f1(tc$ic_li), f1(tc$ic_ls), ci3(rr("p99", "rr"), rr("p99", "rr_li"), rr("p99", "rr_ls")), f1(rr("p99", "temperatura")),
        ci3(rr("p1", "rr"), rr("p1", "rr_li"), rr("p1", "rr_ls")), f1(rr("p1", "temperatura")), f3(min(ct$rr[ct$percentil %in% c("p95", "p90", "p10", "p5")])), f3(max(ct$rr[ct$percentil %in% c("p95", "p90", "p10", "p5")]))), "",
sprintf("Residual heterogeneity was low (Cochran Q = %s, %d df; P = %s; I² = %s%%), and neither meta-predictor was associated with the curve (Wald P = %s for the mean and %s for the range). Concentration-specific MRTs ranged from %s to %s °C; the MRT fell at the 99th percentile in %d of 26 concentrations (Figure 3, Supplementary Table S2). In these %d concentrations, the minimum searched between the 10th and 90th percentiles fell at a boundary in %d (the 90th percentile in %d and the 10th in %d), and its bootstrap 95%% CI spanned the entire search range in %d.",
        f1(h$Q), as.integer(h$df), pc(h$p), f1(h$I2), pc(w$p[w$termo == "media"]), pc(w$p[w$termo == "amplitude"]), f1(min(tb$tmr)), f1(max(tb$tmr)), n_borda, n_borda, p90hit + p10hit, p90hit, p10hit, icfaixa), "",
sprintf("Lag-specific RRs were small in magnitude (Figure 2): at the 1st percentile, the RR was %s at lag 0 and %s at lag 7; at the 99th percentile, it was %s at lag 0 and %s at lag 7. Lag-specific 95%% CIs excluded 1 at lags %s (below 1) and %s (above 1) at the 1st percentile, and at lags %s (below 1) and %s (above 1) at the 99th percentile.", lag_int("p1", 0), lag_int("p1", 7), lag_int("p99", 0), lag_int("p99", 7),
        fmt_l(lags_ex("p1")$lo), fmt_l(lags_ex("p1")$hi), fmt_l(lags_ex("p99")$lo), fmt_l(lags_ex("p99")$hi)), "",
sprintf("If the associations were causal, %s preterm births (empirical 95%% CI, %s to %s), or %s%% (%s%% to %s%%), would be attributable to nonoptimal temperature (forward perspective): %s%% to heat and %s%% to cold; the extreme-heat and extreme-cold components were %s%% and %s%%. The backward perspective gave %s%% (%s%% to %s%%).",
        n_(round(an_t$an)), n_(round(an_t$an_li)), n_(round(an_t$an_ls)), f2(100 * afp("total")$af), f2(100 * afp("total")$af_li), f2(100 * afp("total")$af_ls), f2(100 * afp("calor")$af), f2(100 * afp("frio")$af), f2(100 * afp("calor_extremo")$af), f2(100 * afp("frio_extremo")$af),
        f2(100 * afp("total", "backward")$af), f2(100 * afp("total", "backward")$af_li), f2(100 * afp("total", "backward")$af_ls)),
sprintf("The attributable fraction should not be read as evidence of an association. Its point estimate is biased upward when the reference is the estimated MRT, and its empirical confidence interval does not incorporate the uncertainty of the MRT or the dependence between BLUPs. In this study, none of the pooled relative risks excluded the null, the pooled MRT was imprecisely estimated (its 95%% CI spanned the entire search range), and the MRT fell at the 99th percentile in %d of 26 urban concentrations. In post hoc analyses, a test of the pooled exposure–response curve did not reject a flat curve (Wald χ² = %s, %d df; P = %s), and the observed attributable fraction (%s%%) did not exceed the 97.5th percentile of its distribution under no association in any urban concentration (median, %s%%; 2.5th–97.5th percentiles, %s%%–%s%%; no replicate failed).",
        n_borda, f2(ph$p1$W), as.integer(ph$p1$gl), pc(ph$p1$p), f2(100 * ph$af_obs), f2(100 * ph$resumo$af_total[["mediana"]]), f2(100 * ph$resumo$af_total[["p2_5"]]), f2(100 * ph$resumo$af_total[["p97_5"]])), "",
sprintf("In the key sensitivity analyses (Table 3, Figure 4), the 99th percentile contrast fell within the primary 95%% CI in %d of 6 analyses and the 1st percentile contrast in %d of 6; the exception was %s (RR at the 1st percentile, %s). All six analyses had an interior pooled MRT.",
        dentro99, dentro01, paste(sprintf("lag 0–14"), collapse = ", "), ci3s(fora01$rr01, fora01$rr01_li, fora01$rr01_ls)),
